ang","name_zh":"石敬瑭","born":892,"died":942,"circa":false,"field":"statesman","place":"Kaifeng","place_zh":"汴州/东京（今河南开封）","lat":34.8,"lon":114.31,"known_for":"Founder of Later Jin who ceded the Sixteen Prefectures to the Khitan Liao.","known_for_zh":"后晋高祖，割燕云十六州予契丹。","works":[],"source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shi_Jingtang","source_zh":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E7%9F%B3%E6%95%AC%E7%91%AD","check":{"s":"ok"}},{"id":"guo-wei","name":"Guo Wei","name_zh":"郭威","born":904,"died":954,"circa":false,"field":"statesman","place":"Kaifeng","place_zh":"汴州/东京（今河南开封）","lat":34.8,"lon":114.31,"known_for":"Founder of Later Zhou who began reforms to reduce burdens on peasants.","known_for_zh":"后周太祖，革除弊政，减轻民负。","works":[],"source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guo_Wei","source_zh":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E9%83%AD%E5%A8%81","check":{"s":"ok"}},{"id":"chai-rong","name":"Chai Rong (Emperor Shizong of Later Zhou)","name_zh":"柴荣","born":921,"died":959,"circa":false,"field":"statesman","place":"Kaifeng","place_zh":"汴州/东京（今河南开封）","lat":34.8,"lon":114.31,"known_for":"Able Later Zhou emperor whose campaigns and reforms paved the way for Song reunification.","known_for_zh":"后周世宗，南征北战，为宋统一奠基。","works":[],"source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chai_Rong","source_zh":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E6%9F%B4%E8%8D%A3","check":{"s":"ok"}},{"id":"feng-dao","name":"Feng Dao","name_zh":"冯道","born":882,"died":954,"circa":false,"field":"statesman","place":"Kaifeng","place_zh":"汴州/东京（今河南开封）","lat":34.8,"lon":114.31,"known_for":"Chancellor under five dynasties who sponsored the first printed edition of the Confucian classics.","known_for_zh":"历仕五朝的宰相，主持雕版印刷《九经》。","works":[],"source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feng_Dao","source_zh":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E9%A6%AE%E9%81%93","check":{"s":"ok"}},{"id":"qian-liu","name":"Qian Liu","name_zh":"钱镠","born":852,"died":932,"circa":false,"field":"statesman","place":"Hangzhou","place_zh":"杭州","lat":30.25,"lon":120.17,"known_for":"Foun